        "original_id": "2eae39bd-1c28-5806-b91d-90c5791b6ce7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richard Wagner, Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart, Set Svanholm, Lorenzo Quaglio\n- Works: Siegfried, Der Ring des Nibelungen, Idomeneo\n- Places: Mannheim, Munich\n- Roles: operatic tenor, stage designer\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Wagner composed Siegfried, WWV 86C, as the third of the four music dramas in Der Ring des Nibelungen.\n- Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart composed Idomeneo, K. 366, as an Italian-language opera seria.\n- Lorenzo Quaglio worked mainly in Mannheim and Munich, and he designed the first production of Mozart's opera Idomeneo in Munich.\n- Set Svanholm was a Swedish operatic tenor and was considered the leading Tristan and Siegfried of the first decade after World War II.",
